export const messageInConstructor = "This component declares `state` as a class property while the configuration asks for state to be set up in the constructor. Both styles work; what costs the reader is a codebase that uses each in about half its components, because then finding where a component's initial state comes from means checking two places instead of one. Move the initial value into `this.state = ...` in the constructor.";
export const messageClassProperty = "This component assigns `this.state` in its constructor while the configuration asks for state to be declared as a class property. Both styles work; what costs the reader is a codebase that uses each in about half its components, because then finding where a component's initial state comes from means checking two places instead of one. Declare `state = ...` as a class property instead.";
